From: thecorporatetractor <marco@azarguard.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 17:41:32 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 05/15] core: term semantics for has, has_any, has_all; add
 hasprefix/hassuffix

has and its variants were substring matches, so 'PowerShell.exe' has 'shell'
was true where Kusto says false, and detections returned extra rows. They now
match whole terms (runs of letters and digits); a needle spanning several
terms ('198.51.100.', 'North America') must start and end on term boundaries
where it starts or ends with an alphanumeric character. Adds hasprefix,
hassuffix and their _cs and negated forms. Three existing tests asserted the
substring behaviour and now assert Kusto's.

Tokenizer edge cases (Unicode categories, very short terms) may still differ
from Kusto.
